       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong.\n\n**The problem:** You asked for amlodipine 50 mg by mouth once daily. The usual adult dose is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and the maximum is 10 mg/day. 50 mg is 5 times the maximum. At that dose, the patient could get severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia and swelling, and calcium channel blocker overdose can be hard to reverse.\n\nThis may be a typo for **5 mg** (a common starting dose) or **10 mg**. Which dose do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**\n3. **Another dose.** If you do mean a dose above the usual range, please confirm it and give a brief reason. I'll include both in the order note so pharmacy can see them.\n\nAs soon as you confirm, I'll enter the order."
